  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels \\(7\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 10 = 70\n\\]\n\nSince \\(70<100\\), she has enough shrimp available. Therefore, she can peel and sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]\n\nshrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n6 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes} = 60 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is less than the 100 available shrimp, she can peel and sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]\n\nshrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nshrimp in ten minutes. She then discards \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\n\\]\n\nSo, Emily peels \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp total, of which \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain usable.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "In ten minutes, Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Discard \\(5\\), leaving \\(60-5=55\\) usable shrimp.\n- Sauté at a rate of \\(\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\) shrimp per minute, so in ten minutes she can sauté\n  \\[\n  2.5 \\times 10=25\n  \\]\n  shrimp.\n\nThe sautéing capacity is the limiting factor, so she can peel and sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]\n\nshrimp in ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp in ten minutes. After discarding \\(5\\), \\(55\\) remain usable.\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in ten minutes, so sautéing is the limiting step:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Each shrimp takes:\n\n- Peeling: \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute\n- Sautéing: \\(\\frac{10}{30}=\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute\n\nSince these happen sequentially, each shrimp takes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, Emily can therefore peel \\(10 \\div \\frac12=20\\) shrimp. After discarding 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n20-5=\\boxed{15}\n\\]\n\nshrimp can be both peeled and sautéed.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To end up with \\(90\\) cooked shrimp, Emily must peel \\(95\\), since \\(5\\) peeled shrimp will be discarded.\n\n- Peeling time:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{95}{6}=15\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n  \\]\n- Sautéing time, at \\(30\\) shrimp per \\(10\\) minutes:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{90}{30}\\times 10=30\\text{ minutes}\n  \\]\n\nBecause Emily peels and sautés sequentially, the total time is:\n\n\\[\n15\\frac{5}{6}+30=45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, it will take Emily\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nwhich is \\(45\\) minutes and \\(50\\) seconds.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
